  "answer": "The four deferred-compensation/457 administration and recordkeeping RFPs propose different contract terms:\n\n| RFP | Initial term | Renewal or extension options |\n|---|---|---|\n| [Temple City, California](Temple_City_CA__Recordkeeping-RFP.pdf#page=3) | **Not fixed in the RFP**; to be negotiated after selection. | Vendors are asked to price **5-, 7-, and 10-year** scenarios, but the RFP warns that purchasing rules may limit the initial term to five years. Seven- and ten-year pricing assumes a later extension, **not a guaranteed extension**. [Pricing questions](Temple_City_CA__Recordkeeping-RFP.pdf#page=47) |\n| [Delaware](Delaware__TRE21101-RECDKEEPR-rfp.pdf#page=2) | **Five years**, with the start date to be determined. | **Three one-year options**, exercisable at the Office of the State Treasurer’s discretion, subject to necessary Board approval. |\n| [Monroe County, New York](Monroe_County_NY__10406.pdf#page=6) | **Up to five years**. | **No renewal option is specified.** The committee may cancel at the end of any contract year with 30 days’ written notice; after expiration or termination, it must follow the applicable procedures for awarding a new contract. |\n| [Clark County, Washington](Clark_County_WA__-rfp-955-deferred-compensation-457-plan-administrator.pdf#page=8) | **Three years**, intended to run January 1, 2027–December 31, 2029. | Up to **seven additional one-year extensions** (potentially ten years total), by written notice before expiration. Extension costs are reviewed beforehand; other terms and conditions remain the same. |",
